            <div xml:id="d327">

                <pb facs="0409" n="395" sameAs="frus:frus1944v06/pg395"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/15344</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of War</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Stimson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-04-08">April 8, 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: I have noted your
                    concurrence in the dispatch of General Stilwell’s proposed message to Chiang
                    Kai-shek, subject—Proposed Observers’ Mission to Communist-controlled Areas in
                    China, as contained in your letter of April 4, 1944.</p>
                <p>This matter has been brought to the President’s attention. However, I do not
                    believe final action has been taken.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry</hi> L. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Stimson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
